{# lede #}<span class="text-white">Enterprise Jamstack Wiki Platform</span>&nbsp; for <b>creating, managing, and delivering</b> static webpages using Jamstack Technology for dynamic features therein{# lede #}. For pricing information, see our [Orion Plans](plans).

&nbsp;

### Here's the ROI, Executive Decision Maker :fa-chart-line:...

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Why Choose Orion? The Jamstack Wiki Platform That Outperforms &mdash; and Costs Far Less</span>

&nbsp;

What truly sets Orion apart isn't just another wiki platform &mdash; it's our proprietary Orion Technology, a battle-tested, patent-pending approach that delivers an elegant user experience with unmatched security, reliability and efficiency.

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Nothing will yield better ROI than Orion in the Knowledge Management System market</span>. Unlike the products your competitors are stuck using, Orion is a framework designed to yield superior, maintainable, confidential yet easily locatable corporate documentation with the richest, yet most comprehensible, managed link/dependency network on the market. It turns your organization’s collective experience from a liability that leaks away into your most durable competitive advantage.

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">How so?</span>

&nbsp;

Firstly, by focusing on a handful of industry standard text/source document/data formats, even your most intricate data-generated tables and architectural diagrams are **fully searchable and AI translatable** in any of our supported natural languages. No more lost productivity trying to relocate periodically updated critical infosec details locked in an obscurely tagged, externally generated data table somewhere in your present wiki, and in frustration reaching out to teammates who don't know where it is, which naturally escalates the evolving time sink to managers; and so it goes. Until someone remembers, and because the table is huge and you just want the contents of one element in a single row, you have to fetch and eyeball scan it manually. Then repreat the process whenever you discover that the infosec data is next updated. To add insult to injury, it turns out your existing wiki only renders page contents as a javascript-based web browser application, instead of as a standards-compliant HTML5 document as Orion naturally does.

&nbsp;

Since Orion searches version-controlled sources instead of ephemerally built pages, you will locate the true permalink originals of the material you seek- not amass artificially elevated hits buried in a dozen different peripheral copies of the sought-after information. That externally generated infosec table as above gets incorporated into your Orion wiki as a searchable CSV file attached to an underlying markdown document which otherwise renders it at build time into an embedded HTML5 table. Want to be notified when that attached CSV is altered? Simply subscribe to the CSV file. Upon notification, you can skip the embedded HTML5 rendered markdown page and instead directly fetch Orion's JSON build of its CSV attachment. Convenience, accuracy, and precision, in persuit of the single source of truth, function as major productivity enablers for your most time-constrained employees.

&nbsp;

Orion will surface your once-lost infosec details on demand, and **render it in a manner amenable to the automatable web-enabled/AI agents that your talent prefers**. With unparalleled alacrity and reliability. Want to perfect your search by hand tuning to taste, until you ultimately prefer JSON to HTML5 in your results? Again, Orion delivers (same URL, different headers.)

&nbsp;

Does your current solution? Definitely not, if it's Confluence or Notion.

&nbsp;

Didn't immediately find what you were looking for in Orion's search hits? Refine your current search with a search filter on the material you did locate; repeat if necessary. Or click on a suggested associated keyword generated from the located material to shift your seach in an adjacent direction. Or expand the scope of your search to a higher level in the list of directory breadcrumbs at the upper end of the page. Or switch to a PCRE regex search instead of the Lucene natural-language-stemmed bareword match popularized by Google in its formative years.


&nbsp;

In other words, **information retrieval** is a fundamentally different problem domain than content creation/modification, but the CRUD-based wiki apps from our competitors do not make this distinction in a meaningful way. With Orion's Jamstack design, taxonomies aren't tacked on as an unmanageable generic/emergent afterthought, but with structural planning and consistently enforced, heirarchical organization informed by experienced information architects across your team and ours.

&nbsp;

Next, **content curation tooling** is an essential feature of Orion, not an opportunity to upsell. Our per-wiki facts database is an industry first &mdash; handy for things like managing consistent name branding or related software artifact metadata across the entire website with a 1-line edit to a [YAML file](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/facts.yml).

&nbsp;

So instead of the inevitable, entropic link rot innate to other wiki products, you get **internal/external link validation** at page modification time during a comprehensive, MIME-type based, pre-commit linting pass by Orion's CMS editor. We also provide every customer with a reporting infrastructure to **catch stale internal/external links on demand**, even when the pages involved haven't been altered in months. Diagrams are just as easy to keep consistent with alterations to the prose, because with Orion's mermaid integration, **the diagram sources are embedded in the page's prose** itself. Painless recursive search / replace to repair the associated cruft as it accumulates is built into the PCRE search engine in the CMS.

&nbsp;

Third, as your site evolves to the point where files or folders need to be relocated or deleted, Orion not only tracks location moves by deploying automated HTTP redirects from the original locations to the new targets, but also continues to enshrine the existing ACLs on the original locations in perpetuity. This ensures your confidential content remains protected against historical searches from unauthorized users in the system who might otherwise have direct access to Orion's version control interfaces to your wiki's sources.

&nbsp;

Ever seen a system that can reliably integrate filtered content/data across independent source files?  **Orion can**, with full suppport for the cross-dependencies and authorization controls on each source file.  There's simply no way to launder content through its content integration functionality, and there's no way for content/data in such files to be modified without those modifications percolating down to induce concurrent builds of their dependent files.

&nbsp;

There's nobody else in the industry who has put this much refinement into every aspect of their wiki product as a total package.

&nbsp;

Futhermore, Orion scales with you as you grow, especially at the enterprise level. The $0 per seat licensing and unlimited number of websites opens up new opportunities for knowledge sharing and collaboration across teams, partners, websites, and even the entire planet with our federated platform! We know that for most clients, just a tiny portion of those seat licenses would be used to actually edit pages, but they can use an unlimited number of "associated" read-only accounts in their wikis to share protected information with over the internet. Accounts that need not have any access to the Orion CMS proper- a cost-saving feature unique to Orion as the only corporation-backed **Enterprise Jamstack Wiki**.

&nbsp;

As your personnel's corporate status evolves over time, Orion makes it easy for wiki administrators to deal with the wiki reauthorizations involved. Doing a mass search and replace on every acl setting on the site that's tied to an ex-employee's account is as trivial as onboarding a new staffer or upgrading an existing one by dropping them into the appropriate version-control authorization groups that your team designed.

&nbsp;

In fact, there is **no formal concept of page ownership** in the system. Orion's version control simply tracks the per-user-authorized changesets of staff at the time of the user-committed changes, lending to a more natural, collegial corporate acculturation towards the combined work product of a wiki than in any other similar system. Locking down pages to individual user accounts/"authors" is anathema to the collaborative ideals of wikis, but it is certainly possible moving forward with explicit ACL header assignments on the pages involved.

&nbsp;

Finally, we tailor every installation to your specific requirements, and are **always available for consultation and professional coaching** to ensure you maximize returns on your investment in our products and services. **Your team has a partner in us** in terms of ensuring you see the anticipated productivity gains and customer satisfaction associated with Orion &mdash; designed for robust, verified, collaborative knowledge creation/curation; and easy, comprehensive, precision information retrieval thereof.

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Leave the draining pain points of the past behind...</span>

For a lot of firms, Jira is a wonderfully effective tool for project management. However, over time you begin to realize that [Confluence is just tagging along for the ride](https://projectmanagers.net/top-10-cons-disadvantages-of-using-confluence/)...

If that resonates, are you tired of throwing more good money at a bad investment because of the disjointed, denormalized, unmaintainable, stale, link-rotted Confluence mess with a lousy Text Editor and even lousier Search Engine?

&nbsp;

Don't want to instead waste precious capital on a [performance deteriorating](https://www.reddit.com/r/Notion/comments/1rdals6/is_notion_getting_slower_or_is_it_just_me/) expensive, bloated, [unreliable](https://isdown.app/status/notion), one-platform-to-rule-them-all OCD-lover's SaaS service that cannot fulfill its enhanced productivity promises? In other words, something like Notion?

Prefer the *grokability* of a system like Orion &mdash; organized around *documents with attached data*; instead of Notion's *databases with attached documents*?

&nbsp;

Want a more conservative approach than simply exposing all of your corporate secrets to unscrupulous AI vendors and their ill-gotten frontier models?

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Orion is built for leaders who refuse to settle:</span>

